        { "de": "Untersuchung", "article": "die", "plural": "die Untersuchungen", "en": "examination", "emoji": "🔍", "glossaryKey": "untersuchung" },
        { "de": "Bettchen", "article": "das", "plural": "die Bettchen", "en": "little bed", "emoji": "🛏️", "image": { "type": "svg", "id": "bed" }, "glossaryKey": "bettchen" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Die Pflegerin und die Untersuchung",
        "de": "Das Fläschchen ist klein. Das Büchlein liegt im Bett. Der Pfleger hilft. Die Pflegerin kommt. Die Untersuchung beginnt.",
        "en": "The little bottle is small. The little book is on the bed. The male nurse helps. The female nurse comes. The examination starts."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "-chen, -lein, -er, -in, -ung",
      "practice": "choose",
      "heroTitle": "Die Pflegerin und die Untersuchung",
      "heroImage": "bed",
      "story": [
        "The ending chooses the article. <b>-chen</b> and <b>-lein</b> are a smaller or gentler form, and they are neuter. die Flasche → <b>das Fläschchen</b>. das Buch → <b>das Büchlein</b>. a, o, u and au often take an umlaut. The final -e of Flasche drops. Bett has e, so there is no umlaut: <b>das Bettchen</b>, not Bättchen. die Hand → das Händchen.",
        "-lein is the same idea as -chen, only more southern or a little older. Both are correct. Use the ending the line asks for. Do not trade them.",
        "<b>das Mädchen</b> is neuter because of -chen. One girl: Das Mädchen hat Fieber. The pronoun is es. Several girls: die Mädchen. Not die Mädchens.",
        "<b>-er</b> is the man who does the verb. pflegen → <b>der Pfleger</b>. <b>-in</b> makes the woman, and -er stays: <b>die Pflegerin</b>. Not die Pflegin. der Arzt → <b>die Ärztin</b>, with ä. Not die Arztin. der Patient → die Patientin, and that one has no umlaut.",
        "<b>-ung</b> is the action, and it is feminine. untersuchen → <b>die Untersuchung</b>. behandeln → <b>die Behandlung</b>, not Behandelung. messen → <b>die Messung</b>. der Messer is a knife. das Messing is brass. atmen → die Atmung.",
        "Plural: die Untersuchungen, die Pflegerinnen. A diminutive usually adds nothing: die Fläschchen, die Mädchen. Tabletten is only the plural of die Tablette. It is not -chen, -lein, -er, -in or -ung."
      ],
      "questionRule": "-chen and -lein take das. -er takes der. -in and -ung take die. Keep the umlaut where the pair has one.",
      "tables": [
        {
